1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,729
The examiner arrived with a briefcase, a paperback, and a very stiff manner.

2
00:00:04,729 --> 00:00:22,219
“Sir,” Maya said, “we can examine the method in front of you, if you like.” He wanted to know where the idea came from, and the honest answer was that it came from everywhere and was not particularly helpful.

3
00:00:22,219 --> 00:00:28,334
A fellow in a dark jacket asked how a literary project could claim fluency.

4
00:00:28,334 --> 00:00:31,319
“It cannot,” Lin said.

5
00:00:31,319 --> 00:00:44,579
“But it can locate the point where fluency fails.” A dog barked below the window, someone gave a shout in the yard, and a horse went past with a cart.

6
00:00:44,579 --> 00:00:47,904
A magical claim would have been easier.

7
00:00:47,904 --> 00:00:55,829
A poetic one, a Confucian one, an artistic one: any of them could have hidden the gap.

8
00:00:55,829 --> 00:00:59,879
“Do not boast,” Professor Zhao said.

9
00:00:59,879 --> 00:01:11,989
“A scripture and an X-ray have this in common: neither cares what you believe.” The whisper in the corridor was that the funding had already been decided.

10
00:01:11,989 --> 00:01:22,253
They knelt by the low shelf to weigh the evidence, and a sketchy diagram of their own ancestry of ideas — a map of who had taught whom — lay between them.

11
00:01:22,253 --> 00:01:27,703
“A manipulative summary is worse than a selfish one,” she said.

12
00:01:27,703 --> 00:01:38,963
“At least selfishness is honest.” An editorial in the student paper called the project a quiet success, and by that it meant a small one.

13
00:01:38,963 --> 00:01:49,313
The university senate had asked the same question, and its answer would have to exemplify the existing method rather than replace it.

14
00:01:49,313 --> 00:01:53,098
The arc closed with an unresolved sentence.

15
00:01:53,098 --> 00:01:59,408
“We can manage what we can measure, and we can ignore what we cannot,” Lin wrote.

16
00:01:59,408 --> 00:02:10,108
“That is not a reason to stop; it is a reason to say so.” Such honesty damaged their chances, and they knew it themselves.

17
00:02:10,108 --> 00:02:23,973
The everyday work — a colonized shelf of borrowed books, a damaged sign, a dictation nobody had typed — continued anyway, and a worldwide network of three people is still a network.

18
00:02:23,973 --> 00:02:26,692
A movie would have ended here.

19
00:02:26,692 --> 00:02:29,338
A project does not.

20
00:02:29,338 --> 00:02:34,808
Unless the survey said otherwise, the map itself would stay.

21
00:02:34,808 --> 00:02:50,007
Somewhere between the speech he had prepared and the speech he actually gave, he found the sentence: a knowledgeable reader is not the same as a knowledgeable writer, and an old oriental art catalogue is not a method.

22
00:02:50,007 --> 00:02:54,212
“It has a peculiar magic,” Maya said.

23
00:02:54,212 --> 00:03:04,482
“Do not pronounce it finished.” She asked him to explore the existing shelf and to choose, really, one book for him.

24
00:03:04,482 --> 00:03:13,075
Learning how to learn had cost them a year; the only thing they could show for it was a better question.
